                                "example_id": "d851ddfc-96e5-4624-a02b-d8fc27301ef4",
                                "sense_id": "3cfd173d-7f41-3e2c-a99a-17a67ab8a0e9",
                                "text": "Merc.\n[…]And that in Jove's great dining Room,\nWe were with each one a good thwittle\nAgain set down to swill, and vittle,\nProvided (Signior) do you see,\nThat you should not the Carver be[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26d7da3e-63b6-44a9-8dbe-80c4b97484aa",
                                "sense_id": "3cfd173d-7f41-3e2c-a99a-17a67ab8a0e9",
                                "text": "“Marry, what is't?” cried one fellow[…]“Is't a thwittle shaft?”\n“Ay, or it may be the half of a shuttle,” said another; “dost note, it tapers to the end, and is biggest i' the middle? I warrant Saint Dunstan was a clothier, and made many an ell of stout broella.”\n“'Tis more like he was a butcher,” cried one of that fraternity, “if ye go by likes; for 'tis the very model of a thwittle shaft, and white ash to boot.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a8c4b6e-0f0f-4cdf-b363-f3ba18be8b8d",
                                "sense_id": "3cfd173d-7f41-3e2c-a99a-17a67ab8a0e9",
                                "text": "The butcher stood in the door-way, beating time with his thwittle, and humming[…]"
